# Sits beside the Dockerfile it belongs to, which is what makes it apply. BuildKit resolves
# `--file <path>/Dockerfile` to `<path>/Dockerfile.dockerignore` before falling back to the
# context's own `.dockerignore`, so this scopes the build context for *this* Dockerfile
# without claiming the root `.dockerignore` that other tooling may want.
#
# The header used to describe a root symlink pointing here. There was no such symlink, and
# there had been no `docker/` folder either: the bundle deployed both files to the repository
# root while the workflow and `rhiza-task docker-build` both looked in `docker/`, so nothing
# ever linted, built or scanned the image (#1641).
#
# Patterns below are relative to the build *context* -- the repository root, not this folder.
# See: https://docs.docker.com/build/concepts/context/#dockerignore-files

# Ignore Everything
**

# but don't ignore those files/folders
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!src/

# In those folders make sure those files are not included
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
